  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Anyone pays queued exits from the head of the exit queue, in ID order, until today's outflow\\nwindow is full or `max` exits were handled, and returns how many were. Of an exit that does\\nnot fit, it pays what does, payout first, and the rest stays at the head for the next day,\\nso no window goes unused. The one exception is a payout to an account that does not exist\\nyet, which is never paid in a part below 1 XLM, the least that creates the account: with\\nless room left, release stops and the exit waits for the next day. When the asset contract\\nrefuses a transfer, everything the exit still owes is set aside as a stranded exit for\\n`claim`, so that a recipient who cannot receive never holds up the exits behind it. While\\nthe issuer keeps the vault itself from holding the asset, or the vault holds less than the\\nnext payment, it stops with the queue as it is, and fails with `VaultCannotPay` if it paid\\nnothing. Refused while halted; works while paused.",
      "name": "release",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "max",
          "type_": "u32"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "u32",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
